== Linear forms in logarithms <sec-dio-baker>

#theorem(id: "thm-prime-powers", title: "Prime powers", src: "18.1")[
  Let $x$ be a prime power. The solutions of $b(b + x) = x^n + 1$ with $n >= 2$ are exactly $(x, n) = (3, 2), (8, 2), (3, 3), (5, 3), (8, 3), (64, 3), (7, 7)$.
]
#corollary(id: "cor-x-x", title: "The diagonal $n = x$", src: "18.1")[
  If $b(b + x) = x^x + 1$ has a solution with $x$ other than 3 and 7, then $x > 4 dot 10^9$ is odd, composite, not a square and not a prime power, and the class group of $QQ(sqrt(x^2 + 4))$ has an element of order $d | x$ with $x slash d < 3.3 dot 10^4 ln x$.
]

